From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: rk3528: Set the eMMC's HS200 transmit tap

The RK3528's eMMC host takes the RK3588's driver data, whose transmit
clock tap in HS200 and HS400 is 16. Rockchip's kernel gives the RK3528
its own, 12, and the RK3562 the same. At 16 the HS200 tuning of an
RK3528A box's eMMC failed on one boot in five, the host falling back to
a fixed sampling clock; at 12 it tuned on six boots of six, and its
sequential reads and writes match Rockchip's kernel. Set the SoC's tap.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528.dtsi
index 0f367ef..4389a26 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528.dtsi
@@ -1219,6 +1219,7 @@ sdhci: mmc@ffbf0000 {
 				 <&cru SRST_A_EMMC>, <&cru SRST_B_EMMC>,
 				 <&cru SRST_T_EMMC>;
 			reset-names = "core", "bus", "axi", "block", "timer";
+			rockchip,txclk-tapnum = /bits/ 8 <12>;
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
